00:09:37.700 --> 00:09:38.700
Yeah, Jimmy, listen.

00:09:38.700 --> 00:09:39.700
Those guys aren't my frat brothers.

00:09:39.700 --> 00:09:40.700
I'm here on business.

00:09:40.700 --> 00:09:41.700
Yeah, I know.

00:09:41.700 --> 00:09:42.700
I know.

00:09:42.700 --> 00:09:43.700
Uh, real quick.

00:09:43.700 --> 00:09:44.700
Real quick.

00:09:44.700 --> 00:09:46.700
I was hoping that you could spot me $600.

00:09:46.700 --> 00:09:47.700
Stats.

00:09:47.700 --> 00:09:50.700
A mechanic called the code blue on my alternator.

00:09:50.700 --> 00:09:51.700
Will you work here?

00:09:51.700 --> 00:09:52.700
What are they paying here?

00:09:52.700 --> 00:09:53.700
Shirley Temples?

00:09:53.700 --> 00:09:56.700
They, uh, they let me go.

00:09:56.700 --> 00:09:57.700
Cutbacks.

00:09:57.700 --> 00:10:00.700
I mean, you know what that is.

00:10:00.700 --> 00:10:02.700
I do.

00:10:02.700 --> 00:10:05.700
That's why I'm pretty sure it's not your car that needs to fix, buddy.

00:10:05.700 --> 00:10:11.190
You think that I'm lying?

00:10:11.190 --> 00:10:15.470
I got three bus transfers to prove it.

00:10:15.470 --> 00:10:17.470
Listen, I know a really great place you can go too.

00:10:17.470 --> 00:10:18.470
Get back to being your car.

00:10:18.470 --> 00:10:21.470
yourself is very discreet. Staff's very supportive. Food's great.

00:10:21.470 --> 00:10:24.470
If you're worried about paying for your treatment, don't.

00:10:24.470 --> 00:10:27.470
Because I can take care of that for you, okay?

00:10:27.470 --> 00:10:31.070
Great.

00:10:31.070 --> 00:10:33.070
You're going to drive me there too?

00:10:33.070 --> 00:10:36.419
Because my car doesn't work.

00:10:36.419 --> 00:10:37.419
All right. Hey.

00:10:37.419 --> 00:10:43.659
This road that you're on, man, it is lonely, all right?

00:10:43.659 --> 00:10:49.419
If you need someone to talk to, if you need a friend, then I'm that guy,

00:10:49.419 --> 00:10:54.429
but I'm not going to give you any money for drugs.

00:10:54.429 --> 00:10:59.580
You know, I thought after everything that happened that we could be

00:10:59.580 --> 00:11:04.240
friends. Seeing that you don't trust me, I guess not.

00:11:04.240 --> 00:11:18.179
You've been caring for Davis Bloom in your basement?

00:11:18.179 --> 00:11:21.750
Who else knows about this?

00:11:21.750 --> 00:11:23.750
No one.

00:11:23.750 --> 00:11:27.750
Not even Oliver, and I came to you directly because he can't be trusted.

00:11:27.750 --> 00:11:33.029
Chloe, he created our organization to help with exactly this kind of problem.

00:11:33.029 --> 00:11:38.139
Oliver killed Lex Luthor.

00:11:38.139 --> 00:11:43.639
And the stakes are too high to have someone involved who can't think clearly.

00:11:43.639 --> 00:11:49.049
WebMD doesn't exactly have a lot of intergalactic infection,

00:11:49.049 --> 00:11:50.049
so you were the only person that I could turn.

00:11:50.049 --> 00:11:52.049
person that I could turn to for a cure.

00:11:52.049 --> 00:11:57.340
I am glad that you came to me.

00:11:57.340 --> 00:12:02.340
But there's only so much I can do with a few cells.

00:12:02.340 --> 00:12:04.340
You have his DNA. What more do you need?

00:12:04.340 --> 00:12:09.769
The subject in person?

00:12:09.769 --> 00:12:10.769
That's not going to happen.

00:12:10.769 --> 00:12:17.990
I can run some preliminary tests on the saliva.

00:12:17.990 --> 00:12:25.669
But Chloe, are you sure this is something you want to take on alone?

00:12:25.669 --> 00:12:30.019
I'll be fine. Call me when you get the results.

00:12:30.019 --> 00:12:41.700
Who was that?

00:12:41.700 --> 00:12:43.700
Dave, you shouldn't be outside. What's going on?

00:12:43.700 --> 00:12:45.700
Look at me. It's fine, okay?

00:12:45.700 --> 00:12:46.700
Calm down. It's just.

00:12:46.700 --> 00:12:47.700
A friend.

00:12:47.700 --> 00:12:49.700
Now you know you're not supposed to be out of the house.

00:12:49.700 --> 00:12:50.700
What's happening?

00:12:50.700 --> 00:12:54.370
Nothing else.

00:12:54.370 --> 00:12:56.370
I tried looking at photos of you.

00:12:56.370 --> 00:12:58.370
I tried holding strands of your hair.

00:12:58.370 --> 00:12:59.370
None of it works.

00:12:59.370 --> 00:13:04.370
This thing inside me starts to claw its way out as soon as you leave.

00:13:04.370 --> 00:13:17.379
I can't be away from you now.

00:13:17.379 --> 00:13:20.379
You are now Metropolis's own cornfield killer.

00:13:20.379 --> 00:13:23.379
Now I didn't tell you about this earlier because I didn't want to upset you.

00:13:23.379 --> 00:13:27.379
But the police are hunting for you as we speak.

00:13:27.379 --> 00:13:29.659
And by accepting your help, I put you to help.

00:13:29.659 --> 00:13:31.659
your help, I put you directly in their crosshairs.

00:13:31.659 --> 00:13:33.659
Only if someone finds you, which they won't,

00:13:33.659 --> 00:13:34.659
because I won't let that happen.

00:13:34.659 --> 00:13:36.659
What about when the cops find you?

00:13:36.659 --> 00:13:37.659
What then?

00:13:37.659 --> 00:13:39.659
Then we leave.

00:13:39.659 --> 00:13:48.789
We load up the car and never look back.

00:13:48.789 --> 00:13:59.159
You've done more for me in a few weeks than anyone's done in my entire life.

00:13:59.159 --> 00:14:02.159
But I can't ask you to run away with me.

00:14:02.159 --> 00:14:06.269
That's a good thing you're not the one asking.

00:14:06.269 --> 00:14:25.590
Be able to say goodbye to anyone, not even Clark.

00:14:25.590 --> 00:14:32.009
Obviously tell me that...

00:14:32.009 --> 00:14:46.110
Davis, I would do anything for you.

00:14:46.110 --> 00:14:58.129
This is our chance to start over.

00:14:58.129 --> 00:15:00.129
Let's leave Smallville.

00:15:00.129 --> 00:15:10.070
So this is actually happening.

00:15:10.070 --> 00:15:17.070
Um, I just need to close a few accounts and dead ends and paper trails first, but we can be on the road by sundown.

00:15:17.070 --> 00:15:24.070
Chloe. I know I'd be without you.

00:15:24.070 --> 00:15:52.899
Oliver, I checked the quarry where you said you buried Davis. He's not there anymore.

00:15:52.899 --> 00:15:55.899
Your vision must be getting blurry. I buried that body myself.

00:15:55.899 --> 00:15:57.899
I still have the dirt under my fingernails to prove it.

00:15:57.899 --> 00:16:00.899
I saw the grave. It's empty.

00:16:00.899 --> 00:16:02.899
Why would someone move the body?

00:16:02.899 --> 00:16:04.899
I don't think anyone moved it.

00:16:04.899 --> 00:16:06.899
It doesn't look like anyone dug into the ground.

00:16:06.899 --> 00:16:09.899
Looks like something clawed its way out.

00:16:09.899 --> 00:16:13.570
And that thing's still alive.

00:16:13.570 --> 00:16:15.570
I won't have to Chloe before. I think it may try again.

00:16:15.570 --> 00:16:17.570
Have you warned her yet?

00:16:17.570 --> 00:16:19.570
She thinks I'm being paranoid.

00:16:19.570 --> 00:16:21.820
Paranoid.

00:16:21.820 --> 00:16:24.820
She knows he's obsessed with her, right?

00:16:24.820 --> 00:16:27.820
Which is why I need you to find her. Take her someplace safe.

00:16:27.820 --> 00:16:31.820
I need to head to the fortress, see if I can find a way to send doomsay to a place you can't hurt anyone again.

00:16:31.820 --> 00:16:35.179
No need to pack your parker.

00:16:35.179 --> 00:16:36.179
No need to pack your parker.

00:16:36.179 --> 00:16:40.139
I can tell you how to conquer the beast.

00:16:40.139 --> 00:16:42.139
Kick his ass, Clark.

00:16:42.139 --> 00:16:45.139
Get this thing out of our lives once and for all.

00:16:45.139 --> 00:16:47.139
You want me to kill him?

00:16:47.139 --> 00:16:52.179
No. I need you to kill him.

00:16:52.179 --> 00:16:54.179
We all do. You're the only one who can.

00:16:54.179 --> 00:16:56.179
That doesn't make it right. I'd still be taking a life.

00:16:56.179 --> 00:16:58.179
You'd be saving thousands, Clark.

00:16:58.179 --> 00:17:01.179
The only way any of us are ever going to be safe again

00:17:01.179 --> 00:17:03.179
is if doomsday is destroyed.

00:17:03.179 --> 00:17:04.180
For good.

00:17:04.180 --> 00:17:07.180
Doomsday is my problem and I will handle it.

00:17:07.180 --> 00:17:09.180
Just please.

00:17:09.180 --> 00:17:10.180
Take care of clothes.

00:17:10.180 --> 00:17:22.950
I'm down to my last card, Emil, and I really don't want to play it.

00:17:22.950 --> 00:17:24.950
So please take another look at the samples.

00:17:24.950 --> 00:17:26.950
There has to be a cure.

00:17:26.950 --> 00:17:30.950
His nuclei are in a constant state of mutation.

00:17:30.950 --> 00:17:35.950
I tried to destroy a cell and somehow it got stronger.

00:17:35.950 --> 00:17:37.950
Well, you said you wanted to see him in person.

00:17:37.950 --> 00:17:39.950
I mean, how about I bring him down to your lab?

00:17:39.950 --> 00:17:41.950
Frankly, I don't want him anywhere near me.

00:17:41.950 --> 00:17:45.950
Look, he's not always a monster. I mean, something is keeping him from transforming.

00:17:45.950 --> 00:17:47.950
Well, sometimes...

00:17:47.950 --> 00:17:48.950
Sometimes...

00:17:48.950 --> 00:17:52.950
Dramatic changes to the body are caused by intense emotions.

00:17:52.950 --> 00:17:55.950
Love. Hate.

00:17:55.950 --> 00:17:57.950
Obsession.

00:17:57.950 --> 00:18:05.390
Why my presence stops him from morphing?

00:18:05.390 --> 00:18:11.730
Chloe, this creature puts us all in danger.

00:18:11.730 --> 00:18:13.730
We need to warn people.

00:18:13.730 --> 00:18:15.730
You don't want to do that.

00:18:15.730 --> 00:18:17.730
You betray me, you betray Davis,

00:18:17.730 --> 00:18:20.730
and you sure as hell don't want to be on his bad side.

00:18:20.730 --> 00:18:21.730
Fine.

00:18:21.730 --> 00:18:27.259
But if you do have this power over him, then it's all on you.

00:18:27.259 --> 00:18:28.259
You are the other.

00:18:28.259 --> 00:18:29.259
Only cure.

00:18:29.259 --> 00:18:39.579
Are you just talking to someone?

00:18:39.579 --> 00:18:41.579
Just one of my patients.

00:18:43.119 --> 00:18:45.119
Have you heard from Oliver lately?

00:18:45.119 --> 00:18:49.119
Not since he asked me to hack into a stream of transmissions from Tehran.

00:18:49.119 --> 00:18:53.119
And considering the fact that Farsi isn't exactly my strong suit.

00:18:53.119 --> 00:18:56.119
I should probably get back to translating.

00:18:56.119 --> 00:18:59.589
Chloe Davis is alive.

00:18:59.589 --> 00:19:01.589
I have proof and I need to find him.

00:19:01.589 --> 00:19:04.589
Well, I'm sure that when he resurfaces, we'll hear about it.

00:19:04.589 --> 00:19:08.589
He has a habit of crashing his way onto the 6 o'clock news.

00:19:08.589 --> 00:19:09.589
Well, I intend to find him and bring him to him.

00:19:09.589 --> 00:19:11.589
to the fortress before that happens.

00:19:11.589 --> 00:19:13.589
I got a faint signal from the console,

00:19:13.589 --> 00:19:15.589
and I found the crystal that Brainiac used to release Zod.

00:19:15.589 --> 00:19:20.589
Okay, putting aside my serious distrust of all things, Brainiac,

00:19:20.589 --> 00:19:22.589
how is the crystal going to help?

00:19:22.589 --> 00:19:25.589
He's going to open up a portal to the Phantom Zone.

00:19:25.589 --> 00:19:28.589
Clerk, you can't send Davis there.

00:19:28.589 --> 00:19:30.589
Chloe, he is killed over 50 people.

00:19:30.589 --> 00:19:32.589
He put Jimmy in the hospital.

00:19:32.589 --> 00:19:33.589
There's nothing more I can do for him.

00:19:33.589 --> 00:19:35.589
I'm talking about you.

00:19:35.589 --> 00:19:38.589
I mean, what if when you open the portal, it sucks you in?

00:19:38.589 --> 00:19:39.589
You once told you.

00:19:39.589 --> 00:19:41.589
told me that if there was no other choice,

00:19:41.589 --> 00:19:43.589
that you hoped I would put the good of the world first.

00:19:43.589 --> 00:19:44.589
Exactly.

00:19:44.589 --> 00:19:46.589
And losing you is not good for the world.

00:19:46.589 --> 00:19:48.589
It's a risk I have to take.

00:19:48.589 --> 00:19:55.259
Okay, then maybe I can help.

00:19:55.259 --> 00:19:59.259
I've been hearing about a string of suspicious murders in Alaska.

00:19:59.259 --> 00:20:03.259
I didn't pay much attention to them because they weren't trademark doomsday.

00:20:03.259 --> 00:20:05.259
It's okay, it's a lead. I'll find them.

00:20:05.259 --> 00:20:38.180
Hey, Clark, good luck.

00:20:38.180 --> 00:20:40.180
She's stealing money from Chloe now.

00:20:40.180 --> 00:20:47.619
I guess your car really does need those repairs.

00:20:47.619 --> 00:20:48.619
I'm gonna pay it back.

00:20:48.619 --> 00:21:22.500
Hey, Jimmy.

00:21:22.500 --> 00:21:32.599
Are you okay?

00:21:32.599 --> 00:21:34.599
Aside from being snatched by a crazy serial killer.

00:21:34.599 --> 00:21:38.940
Yeah, I'm great.

00:21:38.940 --> 00:21:41.940
Any idea who did this?

00:21:41.940 --> 00:21:44.940
Not to sound like a broken record, but it was Davis Blum.

00:21:44.940 --> 00:21:55.799
Looks like the talent basement.

00:21:55.799 --> 00:21:56.799
What's he done with Chloe?

00:21:56.799 --> 00:22:10.700
She saved me.

00:22:10.700 --> 00:22:11.700
No way.

00:22:11.700 --> 00:22:14.700
Chloe might be a sucker for the strange, but she's not crazy.

00:22:14.700 --> 00:22:16.700
A bit of advice.

00:22:16.700 --> 00:22:21.269
Really don't want to upset me right now.

00:22:21.269 --> 00:22:22.269
Yeah.

00:22:22.269 --> 00:22:24.269
Trust me, I know.

00:22:24.269 --> 00:22:26.269
I've seen your horns.

00:22:26.269 --> 00:22:28.269
You give a whole new meaning to the term Bridezilla.

00:22:28.269 --> 00:22:49.900
Hey, Davis, it's me. I'm just on my way home right now.

00:22:49.900 --> 00:22:53.900
Chloe, hurry. I can feel myself changing. Please get back here and stop it.

00:22:53.900 --> 00:22:54.900
Chloe, stay away!

00:22:54.900 --> 00:22:59.359
Is there someone there with you?

00:22:59.359 --> 00:23:02.359
Some guys broke into your apartment.

00:23:02.359 --> 00:23:03.359
I'm holding him here.

00:23:03.359 --> 00:23:05.359
Why did you leave the basement?

00:23:05.359 --> 00:23:07.359
Because I thought you were in danger.

00:23:07.359 --> 00:23:12.359
Okay, you trust me, right? So trust me on this and let them go.

00:23:12.359 --> 00:23:15.359
As soon as we were out of Smallville.

00:23:17.359 --> 00:23:19.359
Just come home, Chloe, hurry.

00:23:19.359 --> 00:23:21.359
I'll be there as soon as I can.

00:23:21.359 --> 00:23:34.940
Why did you do it?

00:23:34.940 --> 00:23:45.710
A killer's got a sob story.

00:23:45.710 --> 00:23:49.180
You know, I hear that a...

00:23:49.180 --> 00:23:53.180
Unhappy childhood, that's pretty popular.

00:23:53.180 --> 00:23:55.180
You wouldn't understand.

00:23:55.180 --> 00:23:59.880
Of course not, because you, uh...

00:23:59.880 --> 00:24:01.880
you brooding types, you guys are all so complicated.

00:24:01.880 --> 00:24:05.259
Come on, man, show out.

00:24:05.259 --> 00:24:06.259
No!

00:24:06.259 --> 00:24:07.259
No!

00:24:07.259 --> 00:24:09.259
Monster destroyed my life and brainwashed Chloe,

00:24:09.259 --> 00:24:11.259
and he's trying to ruin hers too.

00:24:11.259 --> 00:24:13.259
You have no idea what Chloe really wants.

00:24:13.259 --> 00:24:14.259
We have to be together.

00:24:14.259 --> 00:24:15.259
Davis. Hey.

00:24:15.259 --> 00:24:16.259
Hey, man.

00:24:16.259 --> 00:24:18.259
Look, I know what it's like to Jones after a girl.

00:24:18.259 --> 00:24:21.259
Really, I do, but you can hold on a little bit longer, okay?

00:24:21.259 --> 00:24:22.259
You have to. Chloe's on her way.

00:24:22.259 --> 00:24:24.259
Oh, I hope so.

00:24:24.259 --> 00:24:26.259
I really do, because if she's not,

00:24:26.259 --> 00:24:29.259
the only way that I can control myself is if I kill one of you.

00:24:29.259 --> 00:24:38.900
Because you've taken everything from me.

00:24:38.900 --> 00:24:40.900
All that's left is scar tissue.

00:24:40.900 --> 00:24:48.750
What are you anyways?

00:24:48.750 --> 00:24:50.750
Because you're sure as hell not you.

00:24:50.750 --> 00:24:51.750
Stop!

00:24:51.750 --> 00:25:05.759
Do you really think that Chloe could ever love you?

00:25:05.759 --> 00:25:10.650
Whatever lies that you told her,

00:25:10.650 --> 00:25:13.650
she's gonna find out the truth eventually when she does.

00:25:13.650 --> 00:25:16.650
Davis!

00:25:16.650 --> 00:25:24.180
Davis!

00:25:24.180 --> 00:25:27.180
Always is never gonna forgive me for that!

00:25:27.180 --> 00:25:28.180
You understand?

00:25:28.180 --> 00:25:31.180
Please.

00:25:31.180 --> 00:25:42.049
Please.

00:25:42.049 --> 00:25:57.869
You mean too much to Chloe.

00:25:57.869 --> 00:25:58.869
It has to be you.

00:25:58.869 --> 00:26:04.710
Davis.

00:26:04.710 --> 00:26:05.710
Sometimes the monster really does get the girl.

00:26:05.710 --> 00:26:07.710
Let's get the girl.

00:26:07.710 --> 00:26:22.859
I'm sorry.

00:26:22.859 --> 00:26:31.950
Chloe?

00:26:31.950 --> 00:26:36.420
Davis, don't do this.

00:26:36.420 --> 00:26:38.420
No! You don't have to do this.

00:26:38.420 --> 00:26:39.420
Oh, her.

00:26:39.420 --> 00:26:46.420
Where are you going to do to me, quick?

00:26:46.420 --> 00:27:30.509
Was Davis holding Jimmy in the basement?

00:27:30.509 --> 00:27:36.900
They're lucky to be alive.

00:27:36.900 --> 00:27:57.799
Jimmy, I'm so...

00:27:57.799 --> 00:27:59.799
You know, Chloe, I thought about calling the police.

00:27:59.799 --> 00:28:02.799
Instead, I figured I'd give you a chance to explain yourself

00:28:02.799 --> 00:28:05.799
before I let them haul you off to prison for harboring a serial killer.

00:28:05.799 --> 00:28:07.799
I shouldn't have left Davis here alone.

00:28:07.799 --> 00:28:08.799
This would not.

00:28:08.799 --> 00:28:11.799
never have happened if I was here, this is all my fault.

00:28:11.799 --> 00:28:16.740
Wouldn't you become one of the bad guys, huh?

00:28:16.740 --> 00:28:23.079
For whatever reason, I calm the beast inside him.

00:28:23.079 --> 00:28:24.079
He needed me.

00:28:24.079 --> 00:28:27.289
He needed you.

00:28:27.289 --> 00:28:30.289
So the needs of the cornfield killer outweigh the needs of the rest of the world.

00:28:30.289 --> 00:28:31.289
Is that it?

00:28:31.289 --> 00:28:32.289
Oliver, it's complicated.

00:28:32.289 --> 00:28:35.289
Yeah, that's the same thing your psychopathic boyfriend told me.

00:28:35.289 --> 00:28:38.289
Look, either I keep him with me or let innocent people die.

00:28:38.289 --> 00:28:39.289
Come on.

00:28:39.289 --> 00:28:44.109
Chloe, if you really believe that, you would have handled things a little bit differently, don't you think?

00:28:44.109 --> 00:28:45.109
Instead, what do you do you do?

00:28:45.109 --> 00:28:47.109
You cook him dinner, you fluff his pillow, you rock him to sleep.

00:28:47.109 --> 00:28:48.109
Okay.

00:28:48.109 --> 00:28:52.609
Look, I understand what it looked like from the outside, but trust me, I had the whole thing under control.

00:28:52.609 --> 00:28:54.609
Chloe, you didn't have anything under control.

00:28:54.609 --> 00:28:59.109
Speaking as Davis's next victim, I can tell you, your plan was seriously flawed.

00:28:59.109 --> 00:29:07.099
How did you think this was gonna end, Chloe?

00:29:07.099 --> 00:29:12.710
I'll find him, okay? I'll fix this.

00:29:12.710 --> 00:29:13.710
No.

00:29:13.710 --> 00:29:18.369
You won't.

00:29:18.369 --> 00:29:21.369
I think you've done enough. We'll let Clark handle it from here.

00:29:21.369 --> 00:29:23.369
Wait, Oliver. Where is Clark?

00:29:23.369 --> 00:29:28.980
He took Davis.

00:29:28.980 --> 00:29:57.000
He's finally going to finish this.

00:29:57.000 --> 00:29:59.000
If this place trapped me once before.

00:29:59.000 --> 00:30:02.000
You want to throw down with me?

00:30:02.000 --> 00:30:03.000
Good luck.

00:30:03.000 --> 00:30:05.000
I don't come here looking for a fight.

00:30:05.000 --> 00:30:07.000
This fortress can help you.

00:30:07.000 --> 00:30:10.569
It's all that's left of our planet.

00:30:10.569 --> 00:30:16.819
How did a piece of Krypton get here?

00:30:16.819 --> 00:30:19.819
My father created it using Kryptonian technology.

00:30:19.819 --> 00:30:23.819
We'll send you to a world where you don't have to hide who you are any longer.

00:30:23.819 --> 00:30:28.579
Without Chloe?

00:30:28.579 --> 00:30:40.559
Because I'm not losing her.

00:30:40.559 --> 00:30:43.559
If you truly cared about her, you would let her go.

00:30:43.559 --> 00:30:46.559
You got it all wrong, Clark.

00:30:46.559 --> 00:30:47.559
She chose to play.

00:30:47.559 --> 00:30:50.559
It was her idea for us to leave Smallville forever.

00:30:50.559 --> 00:30:52.559
Chloe would have done that for anyone.

00:30:52.559 --> 00:30:54.559
She believes in second chances.

00:30:54.559 --> 00:30:59.930
She doesn't actually have feelings for you.

00:30:59.930 --> 00:31:01.930
Why? Because of what I am?

00:31:01.930 --> 00:31:07.400
This Clark, I even killed myself, to try to escape this life.

00:31:07.400 --> 00:31:11.400
But in the darkness, it doesn't come out when Chloe's around.

00:31:11.400 --> 00:31:16.319
She makes me human.

00:31:16.319 --> 00:31:29.329
What happens when that changes?

00:31:29.329 --> 00:31:33.630
It won't. She is my chance to be happy.

00:31:33.630 --> 00:31:35.630
Why can't my own Kryptonian brother let me have very?

00:31:35.630 --> 00:31:37.630
and brother let me have that.

00:31:37.630 --> 00:31:39.630
I'm sorry, Davis, I was wrong.

00:31:39.630 --> 00:32:01.500
We're not brothers.

00:32:01.500 --> 00:32:03.500
I don't want to hurt you, Davis.

00:32:03.500 --> 00:32:05.500
Don't worry.

00:32:05.500 --> 00:32:06.500
You can't.

00:32:06.500 --> 00:32:41.339
I'm taking you with me.

00:32:41.339 --> 00:33:04.930
I can't let you do this.

00:33:04.930 --> 00:33:12.400
This is the right choice, Chloe.

00:33:12.400 --> 00:33:16.029
Trust me.

00:33:16.029 --> 00:33:17.029
Trust you?

00:33:17.029 --> 00:33:19.029
Clark, the only reason why you won't kill him

00:33:19.029 --> 00:33:22.029
is because you don't want blood on your hands.

00:33:22.029 --> 00:33:24.029
I can't believe you are willing to force him

00:33:24.029 --> 00:33:27.029
into a life of hell for all of eternity.

00:33:27.029 --> 00:33:28.029
Clark.

00:33:28.029 --> 00:33:31.029
I know you better than anyone.

00:33:31.029 --> 00:33:34.029
I can't let you do this.

00:33:34.029 --> 00:34:14.760
You would never forgive yourself for giving up on him.

00:34:14.760 --> 00:34:17.760
Tell me that your search team has a read on that beast.

00:34:17.760 --> 00:34:20.760
I have people on every continent, Jimmy, but so far, no.

00:34:20.760 --> 00:34:22.760
No castle, the storm.

00:34:22.760 --> 00:34:30.429
You know, I'm not sure the beast you need to be fighting is out there, Jimmy.

00:34:30.429 --> 00:34:35.159
I think maybe he's in here.

00:34:35.159 --> 00:34:39.159
Look, if this is another attempt to turn me into the poster boy for rehab,

00:34:39.159 --> 00:34:41.159
cancel the photo shoot, because I'm not interested.

00:34:41.159 --> 00:34:43.159
I didn't call here for a lecture.

00:34:43.159 --> 00:34:46.949
Just this.

00:34:46.949 --> 00:34:49.949
It's the money you asked for.

00:34:49.949 --> 00:34:50.949
For your car?

00:34:50.949 --> 00:35:00.860
Forget it. I don't need your handout.

00:35:00.860 --> 00:35:03.860
It's not a handout. It's your first paycheck.

00:35:03.860 --> 00:35:06.860
Oh, let me guess. It's got 12 steps attached to it.

00:35:06.860 --> 00:35:11.860
Well, only if you decide not to take the elevator to your office.

00:35:11.860 --> 00:35:16.860
The truth is, there's an opening on my staff and something tells me you'd be perfect for it.

00:35:16.860 --> 00:35:22.280
I ran a little background check on you. It seems to me there's

00:35:22.300 --> 00:35:25.300
more to your story than you write on your cover letter.

00:35:25.300 --> 00:35:28.300
Unfortunately, what you see is what you get.

00:35:28.300 --> 00:35:31.300
I'm a mediocre photographer turned failed bartender.

00:35:31.300 --> 00:35:36.280
I don't remember seeing a job posting for that on CareerBuilder.com.

00:35:36.280 --> 00:35:39.280
I don't know. Jimmy, everybody knows you take great action shots.

00:35:39.280 --> 00:35:42.280
What I didn't realize until recently was

00:35:42.280 --> 00:35:45.280
when called upon, you're pretty damn good inaction as well.

00:35:45.280 --> 00:35:50.449
You make it sound like I'm some kind of hero.

00:35:50.449 --> 00:36:00.639
I wouldn't be so sure.

00:36:00.639 --> 00:36:04.639
You figured out Davis Bloom's serial killer secret before any of us did.

00:36:04.639 --> 00:36:05.639
You took on the beach.

00:36:05.639 --> 00:36:10.559
beast all by yourself. It takes guts.

00:36:10.559 --> 00:36:12.559
You got good instincts, Jimmy.

00:36:12.559 --> 00:36:14.559
It's enough for me.

00:36:14.559 --> 00:36:16.559
Yeah. Thanks to those instincts.

00:36:16.559 --> 00:36:18.559
My life is really awesome these days.

00:36:18.559 --> 00:36:26.389
Well, if you don't like it, change it.

00:36:26.389 --> 00:36:32.489
Did you start by accepting my offer?

00:36:32.489 --> 00:36:35.489
No, no catch. No catch. Just work.

00:36:35.489 --> 00:36:39.179
And a lot of it. It's a full-time gig.

00:36:39.179 --> 00:36:40.179
What do you say?

00:36:40.179 --> 00:37:14.119
You're looking for Chloe. You're wasting your time, Clark.

00:37:14.119 --> 00:37:17.119
But I guess that's what you do best, isn't it?

00:37:17.119 --> 00:37:22.639
She's gone, man. She doesn't want to be found.

00:37:22.639 --> 00:37:24.639
be found.

00:37:24.639 --> 00:37:27.639
If there's anyone who can make themselves invisible, it's Chloe.

00:37:27.639 --> 00:37:29.639
Davis must have done something to her.

00:37:29.639 --> 00:37:31.639
Chloe would never lie to me if she weren't trapped.

00:37:31.639 --> 00:37:34.639
Either that or she just can't resist tall, dark, and doomsday.

00:37:34.639 --> 00:37:37.639
Besides, Davis isn't a monster when he's around her.

00:37:37.639 --> 00:37:38.639
He's got real feelings for her.

00:37:38.639 --> 00:37:41.639
Whatever his feelings are for her,

00:37:41.639 --> 00:37:43.639
Chloe would never care about him.

00:37:43.639 --> 00:37:48.619
Clark, she sent you on a wild goose chase to Alaska

00:37:48.619 --> 00:37:50.619
when she was hiding that psycho killer in the basement.

00:37:50.619 --> 00:37:56.349
Take it from a guy who spent $10 billion on a merger with the girl

00:37:56.349 --> 00:37:59.349
that got away. You don't always choose who you fall for.

00:37:59.349 --> 00:38:01.349
Chloe, you're talking about does not exist.

00:38:01.349 --> 00:38:04.349
She never choose Davis over her friends.

00:38:04.349 --> 00:38:10.579
People change, Clark.

00:38:10.579 --> 00:38:13.400
It's time you did too.

00:38:13.400 --> 00:38:18.760
You should have killed that thing when you had a chance.

00:38:18.760 --> 00:38:32.349
Clark, I know you want to save everybody.

00:38:32.349 --> 00:38:36.559
But eventually, you're going to have to make the tough decisions.

00:38:36.559 --> 00:38:41.980
It's what heroes do.

00:38:41.980 --> 00:39:18.130
Who is this?

00:39:18.130 --> 00:39:22.130
Clark, it's Chloe. I just wanted to let you know that I'm okay.

00:39:22.130 --> 00:39:24.130
Chloe? Where are you?

00:39:24.130 --> 00:39:28.130
Davis and I are gone, but please don't try and find us, okay?

00:39:28.130 --> 00:39:29.130
We're fine.

00:39:29.130 --> 00:39:30.130
You think that you're safe, Chloe, but you aren't.

00:39:30.130 --> 00:39:32.130
You are not safe with him.

00:39:32.130 --> 00:39:35.130
I'm sure everyone's fitting me for a straight jacket right now,

00:39:35.130 --> 00:39:37.130
but Clark, I do know what I'm doing.

00:39:37.130 --> 00:39:39.130
And I knew that if I told you any sooner,

00:39:39.130 --> 00:39:41.130
that you would have found a way to stop me, so...

00:39:41.130 --> 00:39:47.570
But everything I've ever done, right or wrong, I did for you.

00:39:47.570 --> 00:39:49.570
By running away?

00:39:49.570 --> 00:39:52.570
Admitted Chloe, you have feelings for Davis.

00:39:52.570 --> 00:39:54.570
That's why you're protecting him.

00:39:54.570 --> 00:39:55.570
Clark, I'm protecting him.

00:39:55.570 --> 00:40:00.130
protecting you.

00:40:00.130 --> 00:40:03.130
Condeming Davis to a life as that monster is worse than killing you.

00:40:03.130 --> 00:40:05.130
But what about you, Chloe?

00:40:05.130 --> 00:40:08.130
Chloe, I'm going to spend every second looking for you.

00:40:08.130 --> 00:40:10.130
I will find a way to save you.

00:40:10.130 --> 00:40:12.130
Clark, you're not here to save one person.

00:40:12.130 --> 00:40:15.949
You're here to save all of us.

00:40:15.949 --> 00:40:17.949
And you think sacrificing yourself will help me do that.

00:40:17.949 --> 00:40:22.860
Chloe, you're wrong.

00:40:22.860 --> 00:40:24.860
You're wrong, Chloe.

00:40:24.860 --> 00:40:27.860
I must have thrown a million green rocks away,

00:40:27.860 --> 00:40:29.860
and I have never really saved you.

00:40:29.860 --> 00:40:33.500
Now I can.

00:40:33.500 --> 00:40:37.309
Chloe, listen to me.

00:40:37.309 --> 00:40:39.309
This is your life that we're talking about.

00:40:39.309 --> 00:40:44.059
Don't do this.

00:40:44.059 --> 00:40:48.059
Clark, if there's one lesson I've learned from you,

00:40:48.059 --> 00:40:51.059
it's that choosing the greater good is never a sacrifice.

00:40:51.059 --> 00:40:53.059
Chloe?

00:40:53.059 --> 00:40:54.059
Chloe!

00:40:54.059 --> 00:41:12.280
Hey.

00:41:12.280 --> 00:41:20.280
You said that Roy Tritch could use sweet tooth, so...

00:41:20.280 --> 00:41:22.280
Thank you.

00:41:22.280 --> 00:41:25.280
We better get moving for one at the border by morning.

00:41:25.280 --> 00:41:29.170
Let's disappear.

